# Sibling keys

When a parent element has multiple children (siblings), each sibling must have a `key` that uniquely identifies it **among that sibling list**.

- Keys do not need to be unique across the whole tree — only among siblings under the same parent.
- A single child does not require a key; add keys as soon as there are two or more siblings.
- Do not reuse the same key for two children of the same parent.

```tsx
// ✅ unique among siblings
<Row>
	<Header key="title" value="Hi" />
	<UiBox key="body" uiText={{ value: '…' }} />
</Row>

// ❌ duplicate sibling keys
<Row>
	<Header key="x" value="Hi" />
	<UiBox key="x" uiText={{ value: '…' }} />
</Row>
```

Note: `ButtonImage` `id` is separate from React `key`. Button `id` values used for hover/press state must be unique across concurrent buttons (e.g. `close_${layerId}`).
